# QAAT HTTPS reverse proxy.
# Terminates TLS on each public port and forwards to the plain-HTTP container.
# HTTPS makes the browser a "secure context", REQUIRED for Web Crypto (coordinator
# PWA device key/vault, student check-in fingerprint).
#
# Port-only site addresses (":8443" etc.) mean Caddy serves EVERY host on that
# port — any LAN IP, localhost, 127.0.0.1, or qaat.local — so the stack keeps
# working when the laptop's DHCP IP changes and works fully offline via localhost.
# The frontends derive the API host from the page's own hostname at runtime, so
# nothing bakes a fixed IP. The self-signed cert (certs/qaat.crt) carries the
# current LAN IP + 127.0.0.1 + localhost + qaat.local in its SANs; a brand-new IP
# not in the SAN still works after accepting the browser warning (or regenerate
# the cert). Install certs/qaat.crt as trusted on each device to remove warnings.

{
	auto_https disable_redirects
	# Browsers do not send SNI for bare IP addresses; fall back to the localhost
	# site (same cert + backend) so https://<LAN-IP>:port works from phones.
	default_sni localhost
}

:8443 {
	tls /certs/qaat.crt /certs/qaat.key
	reverse_proxy api-gateway:8443
}

:3001 {
	tls /certs/qaat.crt /certs/qaat.key
	reverse_proxy admin-dashboards:3001
}

:3003 {
	tls /certs/qaat.crt /certs/qaat.key
	reverse_proxy student-portal:3003
}
